  "description": "YUSSEL crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C150 H115 Nd5 O25,2(C7 H8). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1C (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1A (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1B (Nd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.581-5.065 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.86-157.69°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C164H131Nd5O25.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
